  "term": "depth therapy",
  "definition": "Depth therapy is a form of psychotherapy, such as psychoanalytic psychotherapy, that works with unconscious emotions and entrenched maladaptive patterns. In this source, it is described as providing a structured therapeutic approach for processing overwhelming feelings and supporting lasting relational change, especially when early relational trauma is involved.",
